  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tTime and Fees\n\t\tTime and Fees\n\n### Time & Fees: Time (Admin Access)\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Wed, 25 Sep, 2024 at  2:53 PM\n\nThis article will provide a step by step guide on how to log, add and edit the time spent on a particular task specifically for admin users.\n\nRemember as admin you are able to approve everybody’s time including yours and add time from any other account. \n\nAdd time:\n\nNavigation: Time & Fees > Time > Timelog > +Add Time\n\nTo add time you can include the following:\n\nJob ID\n\nClient\n\nTask\n\nUser\n\nDate \n\nTime spent\n\nDescription\n\nOnce saved, it will create a new job and that will be stored in the unsubmitted section.\n\nUnsubmitted:\n\nIn order to submit for approval, you have to hover over the unsubmitted time log and click ‘submit for approval’.\n\nYou can also send reminders here too.\n\nPFA: Pending for Approval\n\nOnce you submit for approval it will be in the PFA section and you can bulk approve/ reject within here. \n\nApproved:\n\nThis then moves into the approved section, which can be seen above and if for any reason you may need to withdraw approval you are able to do this by clicking on ‘withdraw approval’. \n\nOnce you withdraw it moves this back into the unsubmitted section. \n\nRejected:\n\nThis section contains the rejected time logs, if you need to withdraw the rejection hover over the time log and click ‘withdraw rejection’.\n\nYou can also do this in bulk by clicking on all the time logs you need to withdraw rejection for. \n\nNavigation: Time & Fees > Time > +Add Time > Day\n\nAfter adding a job the day view is shown and you can edit the time by clicking inside the time.\n\nAfter adding a job the day view is shown and you can edit the time by clicking inside the time\n\nYou can edit the job after creating it by clicking by clicking on the specific job\n\nYou can also save and submit for approval here\n\nNavigation: Time & Fees > Time > +Add Time > Week\n\nBy toggling to the week view you can select a specific week to view on the calendar.\n\nYou can use the 3 dots on the right hand side to copy previous tasks into the following week.\n\nIf you encounter any issues or require further assistance, don't hesitate to reach out to your Onboarding Manager.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
